## Error reporting

`core/sentry.py`: with `SENTRY_DSN` set, every unhandled exception is sent
to Sentry with its request, tagged with `ENVIRONMENT` and with the request's
`request_id`, so a Sentry issue leads to the request's log lines.
`SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE` (0.1) of requests are traced too. No personal
data is sent unless you change `data_collection`.
